From: RitzDaCat <49771174+RitzDaCat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] core/renderloop: consume the wake sample once per armed wake

The margin controller trains from an armed wake, but nothing in
updateAdaptiveCompositorSchedulingMargin retired the eligibility flag once the
sample had been consumed. Only scheduleNextRepaint set it, and only the
GPU-low-power branch and a full reset cleared it.

Today dispatch() runs once per arm, so no double training occurs. The guard
makes that a property of the function rather than of its single call site, so a
future path that dispatches twice against one arm cannot count one physical
wake as two training samples.

No behavior change in the current call graph: scheduleNextRepaint re-arms the
flag before every wake.

--- a/src/core/renderloop.cpp
+++ b/src/core/renderloop.cpp
@@ -311,6 +311,10 @@
         && desiredWakeTimestamp != 0ns
         && desiredWakeTimestamp == armedWakeTimestamp
         && actualWakeTimestamp >= armedWakeTimestamp;
+    // One armed wake trains the margin at most once. Consuming the eligibility
+    // here keeps a second dispatch against the same arm from counting one
+    // physical wake twice; scheduleNextRepaint re-arms it for the next wake.
+    wakeSampleEligible = false;
     wakeSampleTrained = false;
     if (s_schedulerMarginMode == 0 || !wakeSampleValid) {
         return;
